# Superadmin feature flags (mandatory)

Every **new customer-facing feature or UX** ships behind a Superadmin Ops Deck flag. Default **OFF** unless it belongs in the **Core** or **Trip** pack (first 60s / last 5 min / on-trip logging). No reachable code path when the flag is off.

## Register (all four)

1. `FeatureFlagKey` in `src/types/admin.ts`
2. `FEATURE_FLAGS_META` in `src/utils/featureFlags.ts` — **label + description Superadmin can act on**
3. `DEFAULT_FEATURE_FLAGS` — `false` unless the pack is Core or Trip
4. `CONSUMER_PACKS` `flagKeys` for the matching pack (`core` / `trip` / `travel` / `pro` / `labs` / `ops`)

Bump the flag-count assertion in `src/utils/featureFlags.test.ts`. Ops Deck Flags/Packs are data-driven off this registry.

**Packs (who sees it), not phases (build order):**
- **Core** — first 60s + last 5 min money loop. Default ON.
- **Trip** — voice, receipts, Notes + quiet chat, packing, FX. Default ON.
- **Travel** — passes / Next-Up / scanner / radar. Capable ON; chrome hidden until a pass exists. Route stops stay OFF.
- **Pro** — itemized, OCR, analytics, vault, Splitwise import. Default OFF.
- **Labs** — chat-first, Tripbot, live location, achievements. Stay OFF.
- **Ops** — demo seed, snapshot, sync inspector. Superadmin only.

Do not put settle / UPI / share / clone-squad in Pro. Do not dump new work in Labs unless it is shelved.

## Explanation (required, not optional)

`label`: short name Superadmin sees.
`description`: what the traveler feels **when ON**, what is **absent when OFF**, and what this flag does **not** do (no extra tab, no new product line). One or two sentences. Vague copy like "enables the feature" is not enough.

Reuse an existing flag when the work is the same surface. Do not default-ON Labs or Pro flags to "ship" work.

## Gate in UI/store

Wrap with `isFeatureEnabled('theKey', { tripId })`. Flag OFF = old behavior. Document flags + flag-OFF checks in `docs/FEATURE_TEST_STEPS.md`.
